%% Emulator overview: how vLLM's SimpleCPUOffloadConnector emulates the
%% three-level hierarchy with two CPU memory pools.
%% See docs/design/rfcs/secondary-memory-system-overview.md
flowchart TB
    Acc["Accelerator (e.g. GPU/NPU)"]
    HBM["HBM<br/>(GPU KV cache)"]
    Acc --- HBM

    subgraph Emu["Emulation: two pinned-host CPU pools (M1)"]
        Fast["Pool #0: emulated<br/>secondary fast memory<br/>(pinned host DRAM,<br/>small)"]
        Slow["Pool #1: emulated<br/>slow host DRAM<br/>(pinned host DRAM,<br/>large)"]
        Fast <--> Slow
    end

    HBM <-->|cuMemcpyBatchAsync| Fast
    HBM <-->|cuMemcpyBatchAsync| Slow

    note["Both pools are pinned host DRAM in M1.<br/>No real speed asymmetry — M1 proves<br/>functional management of two address<br/>spaces with small, scoped changes to<br/>SimpleCPUOffloadConnector."]
    Emu -.- note
